          %meta{:content => "application/xhtml+xml;charset=utf-8", "http-equiv" => "Content-type"}/
          %title
          %p This entry compiles pointers related to:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Pierre+Gabriel"}> Pierre Gabriel
                \:
              %p
                %strong Des Catégories Abéliennes
              %p Bulletin de la Société Mathématique de France
              %p
                %strong 90
                (1962) 323-448
              %p
                %a{:href => "http://www.numdam.org/item?id=BSMF_1962__90__323_0"} numdam:BSMF_1962__90__323_0
          %p
            The article (based on a thesis, 1960) develops some of the central aspects of the theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+categories"} abelian categories
            canonized few years earlier by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Grothendieck"} Alexander Grothendieck
            in
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tohoku"} Tohoku
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/localization"} localization
            in the setting of abelian categories (extending ideas of Serre), and the applications to the study of rings and modules (where in V.2. also an alternative reconstructions via
            = succeed "s" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel+filter"} Gabriel filter
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasicoherent+sheaf"} quasicoherent sheaves
            on schemes. It contains a remarkable reconstruction theorem: for any abelian category Gabriel introduces a spectrum whose points are (isomorphism classes of) indecomposable injectives (there is now a refinement using pure injectives,
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Ziegler+spectrum"} Ziegler spectrum
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gabriel-Rosenberg+theorem"} Gabriel-Rosenberg theorem
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/noncommutative+algebraic+geometry"} noncommutative algebraic geometry
